-- title:
--   Fibres of [p^v]_Φ are free of rank p^{vh}
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a commutative ring and $p$ a prime such that $p$ is a non-zero-divisor in $\mathcal{O}$, the ideal $(p)$ is maximal, and $\mathcal{O}$ is complete and separated for the $(p)$-adic topology. Let $\Phi$ be a $d$-dimensional formal group law over $\mathcal{O}$, that is, a family $\Phi_i \in \mathcal{O}[[X_1,\dots,X_d,Y_1,\dots,Y_d]]$ ($i \in \mathrm{Fin}\,d$) with zero constant term, whose linear coefficients in the $X_j$ and in the $Y_j$ are $\delta_{ij}$, satisfying the associativity identity, and assumed commutative ($\Phi_i(Y,X) = \Phi_i(X,Y)$ for all $i$). For $n \in \mathbb{N}$ write $[n]_\Phi$ for the iterated series defined by $[0]_\Phi = 0$ and $[n+1]_\Phi{}_i = \Phi_i([n]_\Phi(X), X)$. Let $h \in \mathbb{N}$ and assume that the quotient of $(\mathcal{O}/p)[[X_1,\dots,X_d]]$ by the ideal generated by the components of $[p]_{\bar\Phi}$, where $\bar\Phi$ is the coefficientwise reduction of $\Phi$ modulo $(p)$, has dimension $p^h$ over $\mathcal{O}/p$. Let $E$ be a nontrivial commutative $\mathcal{O}$-algebra that is free and finite as an $\mathcal{O}$-module, let $v \in \mathbb{N}$, and let $b : \mathrm{Fin}\,d \to E$ have all components in the radical of the ideal $(p)$ of $E$. Then the quotient of $E[[X_1,\dots,X_d]]$ by the ideal generated by the series $[p^v]_{\Phi,i}$ (coefficients pushed forward along $\mathcal{O} \to E$) minus the constants $b_i$ is a free $E$-module, finite over $E$, of rank $p^{v h}$.
--
--   This is the statement that the fibres of the multiplication-by-$p^v$ isogeny of a commutative formal group law of finite height $h$, taken over a point $b$ with topologically nilpotent coordinates in a finite free base change $E$ of $\mathcal{O}$, are finite free of rank $p^{vh}$; for $b = 0$ the quotient is the affine algebra of the $p^v$-torsion level $\Phi[p^v]$, and the content is that the rank does not change at nearby fibres. It is used in the construction of the Hopf-algebra presentation of such a quotient with prescribed comultiplication, via [`MvFormalGroup.exists_hopfAlgebra_presentation_comul_eq_of_cocycle_of_powerDefect`](thm.html#MvFormalGroup.exists_hopfAlgebra_presentation_comul_eq_of_cocycle_of_powerDefect).
